From 51c95d053f921488a723a981280879c0f46dae33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:52:47 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 65/65] PCI: apple-h9p: add T8015 support

The A11 keeps the H9P root complex but changes enough of it that the
T8010 sequence cannot drive it: the common status register is 0x24
(T8010's CTL2), the per-port root complex blocks move to
0x4000 * (port + 1) with the enable, status and reset bits at offsets of
their own. The target speed is a standard LNKCTL2 field, so this SoC has
no root complex link-rate register (iOS: AppleT8015PCIe in the iPhone X
iOS 16.7.16 kernelcache, d221-adt.txt lines 9361-9498).

Add apple,t8015-pcie with its own match data:
- Common init: AppleT8015PCIe's initCommon runs the lane configuration
  and the PHY tunables first, then the port-complex enable, then the
  common tunables; the common status ready bit is polled at rc+0x24,
  followed by the PHY-IP pipe clock handshake (phy-ip+0x74, +0x134)
  before the common tunables.
- Per-port init: the REFCLK bit is cleared before the port is enabled
  and the port's status block has to drain before the enable bit is
  set; the t-refclk-to-perst delay is 100 us on the D221 ADT.
- Config space: every port is a single lane (DWC LINK_CTL/GEN2_CTL x1
  bits); port 3 (the Wi-Fi port) also takes its own lane setup
  (0x8bc set, 0x154 value 0x44444444, 0x8bc cleared). Links that came
  up below the port's maximum-link-speed are retrained with the DWC
  direct-speed-change bit, waiting up to 100 ms.
- Tunables: apcie-phy-tunables go to the "phy" window,
  apcie-common-tunables to the root complex window, pcie-rc-tunables
  to the root port's configuration space and apcie-config-tunables to
  the port block; all from the d221 runtime ADT.

Tested upstream on a d221 (iPhone X GSM): the link trains to L0
(LTSSM 0x11) and the BCM4357 (14e4:440a) enumerates at 5.0 GT/s x1.

Ported from Orchard de95753 / drivers/pci 0030 (the h9p cleanup and the
pwrctrl BCM4357 match were landed earlier as our 0049/0048). Local
delta: has_clocks = false - our T8015 DTB keeps the aux/ref gates as
ps_pcie power domains (converting them to clock-only nodes broke the
ANS2 NVMe on 2026-10-27), where upstream's D221 DTB supplies them as
clocks. This replaces the bare apple,t8015-pcie match entry whose NULL
match data made probe return -ENODEV after the match-data conversion,
and is the root-cause fix for the global PHY init timeout that stopped
the D21 Wi-Fi chain (measured 2026-11-04: h9p reached PHY init and
timed out there on the unported T8010 sequence).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c | 413 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 413 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
